        "original_id": "131a259f-8535-5403-8401-117a2c84a231",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Peverett, David Jack Peverett, Lonesome Dave, Jang Hyun-seung, Hyunseung, Erik Cartwright\n- Bands/Projects: Foghat, Savoy Brown, Zig-Zag Walk, In the Mood for Something Rude\n- Roles: singer, musician, lead vocalist, rhythm guitarist, lead singer, guitarist\n\nFacts:\n- David Jack Peverett was born on 16 April 1943 and died on 7 February 2000.\n- David Jack Peverett was also known as Lonesome Dave.\n- Dave Peverett was an English singer and musician.\n- Dave Peverett was the original lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of the rock band Foghat.\n- Dave Peverett founded Foghat after his tenure in Savoy Brown.\n- Jang Hyun-seung was born on September 3, 1989.\n- Jang Hyun-seung is most often credited as Hyunseung.\n- Jang Hyun-seung is a South Korean singer.\n- On the album Zig-Zag Walk, lead singer Dave Peverett wrote five of the album's ten songs.\n- On Zig-Zag Walk, guitarist Erik Cartwright contributed a sixth song.\n- The previous year's album In the Mood for Something Rude consisted entirely of outside material.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a1a089e0-8574-57af-af00-42bbf33d646c",
        "text": "Page: Dave Peverett. Sentence: David Jack Peverett (16 April 1943 – 7 February 2000), also known as Lonesome Dave, was an English singer and musician, best known as the original lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of the rock band Foghat, which he founded following his tenure in Savoy Brown.\nPage: Jang Hyun-seung. Sentence: Jang Hyun-seung (; born September 3, 1989) most often credited as Hyunseung, is a South Korean singer.\nPage: Zig-Zag Walk. Sentence: Unlike the previous year's \"In the Mood for Something Rude\", which consisted of all outside material, lead singer Dave Peverett wrote five of the album's ten songs, with guitarist Erik Cartwright contributing a sixth.",
